  PARITY FIX (recommended-range unit bug, documented not silently dropped — Honesty rule 9):
    The web computes the reference-line positions as `toPressureValue(RECOMMENDED_RANGE_BAR.low *
    100_000)` (2.4 bar * 100_000). `toPressureValue` / `convertPressureFromSI` consume SI **kilopascals**
    (the Phase-42 floor — confirmed by the backend contract + the LiveSignals widget tests
    `convertPressureFromSI(100,.bar)==1`, `(250,.psi)==250/6.894757`), so the correct bar->kPa factor is
    *100 (2.4 bar = 240 kPa), NOT *100_000. The web factor is 1000x too large, pushing the Min/Max lines
    ~1000x above any real reading (off the top of the plot, effectively invisible). This native port uses
    the correct kilopascal magnitudes (240 / 280 kPa) so the recommended band renders ON-SCALE with the
    data, both converted through the SAME TirePressureConvert path. The Min/Max feature (explicit i18n
    keys) is reproduced and made functional rather than ported broken.

